    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d02fbeb8_7fe4dee3",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 234,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-23T02:32:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is already G3 state when this code is executed, So it wouldn\u0027t force the APP off earlier for SKU 70/71. The purpose here is for this scenario: 1.The unit power off. 2.EC enter G3 state. 3.The SOC is 4% and 1 hour has passed. 4. EC enter hibernate mode(we want to prevent this step from happening here otherwise it seems no chance to cutoff battery)",
      "parentUuid": "a2c5b16f_dfe06fd4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 228,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 234,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "1fbb3d4e3209245252842834d2a3c7ffff12bbd2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0343bf6_82dc830a",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 234,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-28T23:04:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How long are we delaying hibernate for? Does it never hibernate when the SOC is \u003c 4%. \n\nMy other concern here is that I think this should have a config option guard as other boards won\u0027t have the function battery_is_cutoff_required() defined and so those builds will fail. I know this is a coral FW branch, but I don\u0027t think we should break builds for other boards.",
      "parentUuid": "d02fbeb8_7fe4dee3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 228,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 234,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "1fbb3d4e3209245252842834d2a3c7ffff12bbd2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
